# test coverage & mutation testing
coverage
.stryker-tmp
test-metrics/
# ...but keep the small, diffable coverage summary committed as an additive baseline
# trail, so coverage movement is reviewable in a PR diff. Everything bulky or
# regenerated stays ignored above and is published by CI as a build artifact instead:
# HTML reports, lcov, and the Stryker JSON (~700KB on a single line, so it neither
# diffs nor deltas). Note the Stryker incremental cache lives in .stryker-tmp/, not
# here. Enforcement is the vite.config.ts coverage thresholds and Stryker's `break`.
!test-metrics/
!test-metrics/coverage/
test-metrics/coverage/*
!test-metrics/coverage/coverage-summary.json
test-metrics/mutation/
